{% if part == "LyricsWikifonia" %}\lyricmode {
	Oh, I woke me up this morn -- ing and I heard a joy -- ful song From the throats of hap --
	py Ir -- ish -- men, a hun -- dred thou -- sand strong. Shure it was the Hi -- ber -- ni --
	an Bri -- gade __ lin -- ing up for to start the big par -- ade. __ So I fetch'd me Sun --
	day bon -- net and the flag I love so well, And I bought me -- self a sham -- rock just to
	wear in me la -- pel. Don't you know that to -- day's March sev -- en -- teen? __ It's the
	day for the wear -- ing of the green. __ It's a great day __ for the I -- rish, __ it's a
	great day for the fair. __ The side -- walks of New York are thick with blar -- ney __ For
	shure you'd think New York was Old Kil -- ar -- ney. __ It's a great day __ for the sham --
	rock __ for the flags in full ar -- ray __ We're fee -- ling so in -- spir -- ish, shure
	be -- cause for all the I -- rish, It's a great, great __ day! It's a day! __
}
